{"images":["data:image/webp;base64,"],"messages":[{"content":"The bar has a cross-sectional area A and is subjected to the axial load P. Determine the average normal stresses acting over the shaded section, which is oriented at $\\theta$ from the horizontal. <image>\n\n(A) P/(A)*sin(2$\\theta$)\n(B) (P/A)sin^2($\\theta$)\n(C) P/(2A)*sin(2$\\theta$)\n(D) (P/2A)sin^2($\\theta$)\n\nAnswer with the option's letter from the given choices directly.","role":"user"}]}